    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/09/mizuno-wave-rebellion-flash-3-review.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The dual-layer ENERZY XP (TPEE) + ENERZY NXT (EVA) midsole feels soft and bouncy with plenty of heel and forefoot protection, and the large heel bevel helps roll/pivot forward for midfoot or forward-heel landings.",
        "Responsiveness: Foam rebound plus the nylon wave plate produce good energy return, with smooth easy-pace transitions and a notably snappier, bouncier feel at uptempo/tempo paces.",
        "Stability: The glass fiber-infused nylon plate and wider base add structure to the soft platform, but stability is mixed due to reported medial bias and a slightly flexible heel counter with minimal rearfoot padding.",
        "Durability: Overall durability is rated high, with an above-average durability expectation in the review."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/09/mizuno-wave-rebellion-flash-3-review-3.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: High stack cushioning (37.5/34.5 mm, with a very thick heel section) feels very soft and protective with a super-bouncy underfoot feel, though the heel does not feel sink-in plush and the geometry drives a forward roll.",
        "Responsiveness: A major strength - the ENERZY XP foam plus glass-fiber plate is described as lively, explosive, and propulsive, with strong energy return and quick toe-offs in workouts.",
        "Stability: Clear weak point - heel stability is limited and medial midfoot support is lacking, with reports of inward ankle collapse/overpronation tendency and some ankle soreness, even though the plate/EVA setup adds some baseline control.",
        "Durability: The blown-rubber outsole is intended for training durability and showed good grip on multiple surfaces; early feedback suggests decent longevity, but long-term outsole wear data is limited in this review."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/mizuno-wave-rebellion-flash-3-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: High-stack (51 mm heel / 48 mm forefoot) dual-layer Enerzy XP + Enerzy NXT gives plenty of cushioning and strong impact protection, but the ride favors forefoot loading and can feel brake-like on heel landings as fatigue sets in.",
        "Responsiveness: The foam mix provides noticeable bounce and enough energy return to pick up pace, though it is described as less ideal when maximum speed/snappiness is required.",
        "Stability: The Flash 3 is said to add a touch more stability than the Pro setup, but lateral/overall stability is highly geometry-dependent and works best for forefoot strikers; detailed torsional and heel-counter stiffness data is not provided.",
        "Durability: The thicker unnamed outsole rubber is highlighted as likely more durable for accumulating longer miles versus a weight-saving race-oriented compound, with no major material-longevity complaints noted."
      ]
    }
  ],
